[  16084s] headline: In season a rookie's own tracking quickly dominates: for the 9 reliably measured traits his qualifying games outweigh any pre-season prior after 2-7 games. On 2025 rookies (pseudo-prospective: fit on the 2023-24 seasons only), shrinking early games toward the position average does almost all the work: it achieves 99% of the preregistered blend's 72% error cut after one game (H1). Adding the stopwatch and draft slot to the prior lowers error a further 5% before the first game (post hoc, p 0.03, BH q 0.29) and 2.5% after one game; Combine tracking adds nothing (H3 error ratio 1.021 [1.004, 1.039], slightly worse).
